    "why": "Bottom-up processing starts at the bottom of the system, where energy from the environment stimulates the receptors. It is also called data-driven processing. When a person looks at a woman named Mary, the sequence is light reflected from Mary, then an image on the retina, then signals in the optic nerve, then signals in the brain. In general the sequence is stimulus, receptors, neural signal and representation."
