    "correct": 0,
    "why": "Prägnanz, also called simplicity or good figure, means that a pattern is organized so the result is as simple as possible. The Olympic symbol is seen as five overlapping circles. It is not seen as nine irregular closed shapes fitted together, although that also fits the lines."
